    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2007-04-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2007-06-01"></period-end>
     <target value="US$110 million"></target>
     <actual value="$130 million">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">CCRIF retained $20 million of risk and secured reinsurance for additional losses up to $130 million (CCRIF took slightly more than$2 million of the first and second layers of reinsurance).  This gives CCRIF the capacity to withstand a series of catastrophicevents having a probability of occurring only once in 1000 years.  CCRIF has shareholder equity and other assets on top of thisthat would give it the capacity to withstand a series of events with a probability of occurring only once in 10,000 years.  CCRIFwould, however, need to be recapitalized thereafter in order to continue operations.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
